# The graphics console (display driver plan, phase G1): on QEMU's standard
# graphics card the bochs driver sets 1920x1080 at boot, and text is drawn
# with the built-in font. The screenshots check what a monitor would show.
# The desktop is off here: this is about the full-screen console.
@args desktop=off
$ display
driver: bochs
mode: 1920x1080, 32 bits per pixel
text: 240x67 characters (8x16 font, automatic)
@screenshot 1920x1080 text

# Color bars cover the whole screen; Enter brings the text back.
$& display test
@screenshot 1920x1080 bars
> x
$wait
color bars on the screen: press Enter to go on
~ ^drawing the whole screen again took \d+\.\d ms$
@screenshot 1920x1080 text

# Another resolution; the console follows.
$ display mode 1280x720
driver: bochs
mode: 1280x720, 32 bits per pixel
text: 160x45 characters (8x16 font, automatic)
@screenshot 1280x720 text
$ echo still typing: héllo
still typing: héllo
$& display test
@screenshot 1280x720 bars
> x
$wait

# Sizes the card or the kernel cannot do leave the mode as it is.
$ display mode 4096x2160
display mode 4096x2160: too large for the card's video memory
$ display mode 100x100
display mode 100x100: not a usable size (320x200 to 4096x2160, e.g. 1920x1080)
$ display mode 1280x720x32
~ not a usable size
$ display speed
~ ^drawing the whole screen again takes \d+\.\d ms \(best of 5\)$
~ ^of which copying to video memory: \d+\.\d ms$
$ display mode
usage: display [mode WIDTHxHEIGHT | font 1|2|auto | test | speed]
$ display
mode: 1280x720, 32 bits per pixel
@screenshot 1280x720 text

# A long output scrolls; the screen survives it.
$ help
~ ^  display \[mode WxH\]
$ help
$ help
$ display mode 1920x1080
text: 240x67 characters (8x16 font, automatic)
@screenshot 1920x1080 text
